{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QGeometricLanglands.ModularSTransformQQTilde","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QGeometricLanglands.ModularSTransformQQTilde","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ModularSTransformQQTilde.s_automorphy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ModularSTransformQQTilde.s_automorphy","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/modular-s-transform-q-q-tilde.lean#L122-L122","doc":"D14 conjecture: on the upper half-plane, `F` is `S`-covariant with the\nJacobi-theta automorphy factor, `F(-1/τ) = (-iτ)^{1/2} · F(τ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ModularSTransformQQTilde.nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ModularSTransformQQTilde.nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/modular-s-transform-q-q-tilde.lean#L119-L119","doc":"Non-triviality: `F` does not vanish identically on the upper half-plane,\nso the `S`-duality is not vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ModularSTransformQQTilde.F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ModularSTransformQQTilde.F","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/modular-s-transform-q-q-tilde.lean#L116-L116","doc":"Conjectural modular continuation of the Hecke-parameter data, on `ℂ`\n(used on the upper half-plane `Im τ > 0`, i.e. the bar-image branch). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ModularSTransformQQTilde.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ModularSTransformQQTilde.mk","kind":"ctor","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/modular-s-transform-q-q-tilde.lean#L113-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ModularSTransformQQTilde","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ModularSTransformQQTilde","kind":"class","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/modular-s-transform-q-q-tilde.lean#L101-L123","doc":"**CONJECTURE (D14, §3b-cond axiomatisation).**  Modular $S$-transform\n$q \\leftrightarrow \\tilde q = \\exp(-2\\pi i/\\tau)$ for Hecke-parameter analytic\ncontinuation.\n\nThe class axiomatises the conjectural *hypotheses* of D14 (not its\nconclusion): a modular continuation `F` of the framework's Hecke data to the\nupper half-plane, which is **non-degenerate** and is **`S`-covariant** with the\nJacobi-theta automorphy factor `(-iτ)^{1/2}` under `S : τ ↦ -1/τ`.  An instance\nis the conjectural witness (sorry = conjecture); the canonical analytic\ninhabitant is Mathlib's `jacobiTheta` via `jacobiTheta_S_smul`.  The residual\nassembly conjecture — that the framework's Hecke data *is* such a theta — stays\nopen and is carried by the instance. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:modular-s-transform-q-q-tilde","label":"conj:modular-s-transform-q-q-tilde","md":"quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/modular-s-transform-q-q-tilde.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s_image_in_upper_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s_image_in_upper_half","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/modular-s-transform-q-q-tilde.lean#L90-L99","doc":"**The modular `S`-transform preserves the convergent (bar) domain (proved).**\nThe D14 map `S : τ ↦ -1/τ` keeps `Im τ > 0`, i.e. the theta-convergent\nupper-half-plane branch — the bar-side branch on which the substrate enters via\nits image `q₀⁻¹` (see `bar_image_in_upper_half`) — is `S`-stable.  So the D14\nduality is a well-defined self-map of the domain where the theta sector\nconverges, not a map off it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bar_image_in_upper_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bar_image_in_upper_half","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/modular-s-transform-q-q-tilde.lean#L79-L88","doc":"**Bar image lands in the upper half-plane (proved).**  The bar image\n`q₀⁻¹ < 1` of a real substrate `q₀ > 1` *is* in the theta convergence domain:\nthe modular parameter `τ₀` with `exp(2πiτ₀) = q₀⁻¹` has `Im τ₀ > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.real_value_in_disk_in_upper_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.real_value_in_disk_in_upper_half","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/modular-s-transform-q-q-tilde.lean#L69-L77","doc":"**A real value in the unit disk lands in the upper half-plane (proved).**\nIf a real Hecke value `r ∈ (0,1)` equals the nome `exp(2πiτ₀)`, then `Im τ₀ > 0`\n— i.e. `τ₀ ∈ ℍ`, the theta convergence domain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.substrate_not_in_upper_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.substrate_not_in_upper_half","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/modular-s-transform-q-q-tilde.lean#L55-L67","doc":"**Substrate bar-side corollary (proved).**  A real Hecke value `q₀ > 1` is\noutside the theta convergence domain: the modular parameter `τ₀` with\n`exp(2πiτ₀) = q₀` is **not** in the open upper half-plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.theta_nome_norm_lt_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.theta_nome_norm_lt_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/modular-s-transform-q-q-tilde.lean#L38-L53","doc":"**Theta-convergence invariant (proved).**  The Jacobi theta nome\n`exp(2πiτ)` lies in the open unit disk — the convergence domain of the theta\nseries `∑_{n∈ℤ} z^n q^{n²}` — **iff** `τ` lies in the open upper half-plane\n`Im τ > 0`.\n\nThis is the formalize-first invariant of the Jacobi-triple-product avenue: it\npins the framework's modular / theta sector to the substrate's *bar image*\n`q₀⁻¹ < 1` (because the real substrate `q₀ ≈ 1.11 > 1` forces `Im τ₀ < 0`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}